    {
      "title": "Home",
      "slug": "home",
      "content": "Shivaji University, Kolhapur is one of the oldest and premier universities in India, established in 1962. It is named after the great Maratha warrior king Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj.",
      "sections": [
        {
          "__component": "sections.hero-section",
          "subheading": "Shaping Bright Minds Through Quality Education",
          "heading": "Shivaji University: \nEmpowering Future Generations",
          "buttonText": "Admissions Open",
          "buttonLink": "/admissions"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "About Us",
      "slug": "about-us",
      "content": "Established in 1962, Shivaji University, Kolhapur is a leading state university in Maharashtra. It offers a wide range of undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral programmes across faculties of Science and Technology, Commerce and Management, Humanities, and Inter Disciplinary Studies."
    },
    {
      "title": "About Kolhapur City",
      "slug": "About-Kolhapur",
      "content": "",
      "sections": [
        {
          "__component": "sections.hero-banner",
          "title": "ABOUT SUK"
        },
        {
          "__component": "sections.content-with-image",
          "title": "About Kolhapur City",
          "content": "Kolhapur is famous for being a centre of Art, education, Industry and sports, particularly wrestling. Here the wrestling is called as \"Kusti\" and wrestlers are known as \"Malla\". This wrestling match is played in the square clay ground which is known as \"Akhada\".\n\nSimilar to \"The Operation Flood\" project in Gujrat, in Kolhapur the \"Warna Project\" was started and till date is famous for huge amount of generation of milk and milk products which are transported to the all over of India.\n\nKolhapur comes under sugarcane belt and because of this people are very rich and live prosperous life.\n\nKolhapuri chappals are renowned for their durability and beauty of make.",
          "imagePosition": "none"
        },
        {
          "__component": "sections.content-with-image",
          "title": "Reaching Kolhapur City",
          "content": "As it is an important journey station from Bombay to Goa via Pune, the Ujalaiwadi airport is 10 km away from Kolhapur main city. One can also travel from Kolhapur to major cities like Pune, Mumbai, Delhi, and Bangalore.\n\nState Transport Corporation operates buses for all major cities from Kolhapur to all over Maharashtra, Karnataka, and Goa.\n\nPrivate buses and travels operates luxury and AC services for all over Maharashtra, Karnataka, and Goa.",
          "imagePosition": "none"
        },
        {
